    {
      "title": "Split the fraction into powers",
      "body": "<p>The denominator is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Divide each numerator term by this power separately, using <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msup><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "A radical in a denominator can be rewritten as a fractional negative power.",
      "pitfall": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Write the two powers that remain after dividing the numerator.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l20",
          "reminder": "A radical in a denominator can be rewritten as a fractional negative power."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Apply the power rule to both terms",
      "body": "<p>The integrand is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Increase each exponent by 1 and divide its coefficient by that new exponent.</p>",
      "recap": "Integrate a sum term by term, retaining each coefficient and sign.",
      "pitfall": "The new exponents are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>; neither term requires a logarithm.",
      "pause": "Find the antiderivative before substituting either limit.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l20",
          "reminder": "Integrate a sum term by term, retaining each coefficient and sign."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Apply the limits to your result",
      "body": "Evaluate your antiderivative at the upper limit and subtract its value at the lower limit.",
      "recap": "A definite integral is a signed value, calculated by upper value minus lower value.",
      "pitfall": "Keep brackets around the entire lower-limit value.",
      "pause": "Integrate the powers yourself, then substitute both limits and simplify exactly.",
      "recall": [
