  "solution": "<p><strong>1. Rewrite the integrand.</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2. Integrate the powers.</strong> An antiderivative is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>3. Apply the limits.</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x000D7;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x000D7;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math>. Thus the integral is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer D.</strong> A definite integral may be negative; do not replace it by a positive area.</p>",
